## Google Maps scraper for lead generation — Playwright + Python on Oracle Linux 9 aarch64

### What was built

A standalone Python scraper (`/tmp/gmaps_scraper.py`) that uses Playwright Chromium to extract business listings from Google Maps for outreach: name, address, phone, website, rating, review count.

### Dependencies (all pre-installed on this host)

- `playwright` (Python) — already in Hermes venv: `pip3 install playwright`
- Chromium browser — `python3 -m playwright install chromium` (downloads ARM fallback build)
- `requests` — pre-installed

### Verified install sequence

```bash
# Install playwright Python package (if not present)
pip3 install playwright

# Install Chromium browser for playwright
python3 -m playwright install chromium
# On Oracle Linux 9 aarch64 this downloads a fallback ubuntu24.04-arm64 build

# Verify
python3 -c "from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright; print('Playwright ready')"
```

### Running the scraper

```bash
# Single keyword, 10 results
python3 /tmp/gmaps_scraper.py "coffee shops in New York" -n 10

# Multiple keywords, save to specific file
python3 /tmp/gmaps_scraper.py \
  "restaurants in New York" \
  "law firms in New York" \
  "real estate agencies in New York" \
  -n 15 --wait 3 \
  -o /home/opc/leads/all_leads.csv
```

### CLI options

| Flag | Default | Meaning |
|------|---------|---------|
| `-n, --max` | 50 | Max results per keyword |
| `-o, --output` | auto (CSV in /tmp/gmaps-leads/) | Output file path |
| `--json` | False | Output JSON instead of CSV |
| `--visible` | False | Show browser window (debugging) |
| `-w, --wait` | 5 | Seconds between keywords |
| `--delay` | 1.5 | Scroll delay in seconds |

### What it extracts per business

`name, keyword, address, phone, website, rating, reviews, category, source, scraped_at`

### Output format

- CSV (default) + JSON copy in same directory
- Merged master file: concatenate all CSVs, deduplicate by (name, keyword)

### Known limitations

- Google Maps blocks automated browsers — the scraper handles captcha detection but may fail on aggressive scraping
- Phone/website extraction requires clicking into each business detail page (slower, limited to 20 per keyword by default)
- Address extraction from card view is heuristic — may miss or misparse
- Rate limiting: use `--wait` between keywords to avoid blocks

### Common failure modes

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| `Timeout waiting for results` | Google blocking or slow load | Increase timeout, add `--wait`, try different keyword |
| `Captcha/block detected` | Too many requests from IP | Wait, use different IP, reduce rate |
| `No results and no block page` | Selector mismatch (Google changed DOM) | Inspect `div[role="article"]` count; update selectors |
| 0 phone/website | Card view doesn't show details | Click into each business (already implemented, limit 20) |

### Architecture notes

- Playwright Chromium launched with `--no-sandbox`, `--disable-dev-shm-usage`, `--disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled`
- User agent spoofed to desktop Chrome 120
- Search directed to `https://www.google.com/maps/search/<keyword>` (not the Maps homepage)
- Results loaded by scrolling; extraction from `div[role="article"]` elements
- Detail page visit: click card → wait 3s → extract phone/website → go back

### File locations

- Scraper script: `/tmp/gmaps_scraper.py`
- Leads output dir: `/tmp/gmaps-leads/` (per-keyword CSV+JSON)
- Merged master: `/home/opc/leads/all_leads.csv`
